# Fedora optional/build package list for Omarchy quattro
# Format: one package name per line
#
# These are the packages from omarchy-other.packages mapped to Fedora equivalents, plus the
# build tooling the git-clone install needs. Everything x86- or Arch-only is omitted below.

@development-tools
autoconf-archive
btrfs-progs
egl-wayland
pipewire-gstreamer
gtk4-layer-shell
pulseaudio-libs
tiny-dfr
glycin-loaders
wget2-wget
zram-generator

# Omitted/handled elsewhere:
# - pipewire, pipewire-alsa, pipewire-jack, pipewire-pulse: preinstalled on Fedora Asahi
# - webp-pixbuf-loader: retired in Fedora 44. gdk-pixbuf2 carries an Obsoletes tag for it, so the
#   name still resolves, but nothing in Fedora 44 ships a webp gdk-pixbuf loader. Image decoding
#   for GTK4 apps moved to glycin, so glycin-loaders above is what actually renders webp.
# - snapper: in the base list
# - iwd: dropped. The installer used to swap NetworkManager's wifi backend to iwd at the very end
#   (post-install/network-finalize.sh), which orphaned the connection the install itself was made
#   over: the profile NetworkManager saved through wpa_supplicant kept rejecting the correct
#   password afterwards, because iwd has none of its credentials. hardware/network.sh disables
#   iwd.service anyway, so the two steps contradicted each other. NetworkManager keeps its default
#   wpa_supplicant backend, as in 3.8.3 (whose install.sh never ran the finalize step).
# - tiny-dfr: Touch Bar daemon - relevant on M1/M2 MacBook Pro 13" under Fedora Asahi
# - limine, limine-mkinitcpio-hook, limine-snapper-sync, linux, linux-headers, linux-firmware,
#   base, base-devel, dkms, yay-debug: Arch boot/packaging stack - Fedora Asahi boots via its own
#   kernel and dracut, and @development-tools replaces base-devel
# - kernel-modules-hook, qemu-user-static-binfmt: Arch-only; Fedora uses akmods and systemd binfmt
# - nvidia-* (all), lib32-nvidia-*, intel-ipu7-camera, intel-lpmd, intel-media-driver,
#   libva-intel-driver, libva-nvidia-driver, libvpl, vpl-gpu-rt, vulkan-intel, vulkan-radeon,
#   thermald, sof-firmware, broadcom-wl, asusctl, dell-xps-touchpad-haptics, linux-ptl*,
#   linux-t2*, t2fanrd, apple-bcm-firmware, apple-t2-audio-config (T2 = Intel Macs),
#   tuxedo-drivers-nocompatcheck-dkms, yt6801-dkms, qmk-hid, macbook12-spi-driver-dkms,
#   linux-firmware-marvell: x86-only hardware - never present on Apple Silicon
# - vulkan-asahi: Fedora ships Vulkan in mesa-vulkan-drivers (base list)
